            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Clematicissus striata is a species of climbing plant in the family Vitaceae. The plant is found in south-central Chile (Coquimbo to Magallanes regions), Argentina, Brazil, Uruguay, Paraguay and Bolivia. It has a woody stem that looks reddish as it ages. Its leaves are composed by five folioles in a palmated shape."
